## Methods used today

### Manual bad-channel review
A structured visual review was performed across Standard, Pitch Deviant, and Duration Deviant trials. The working rule was:

> Mark a channel as bad if it appeared abnormal in approximately 50% of inspected trials and appeared across more than one condition type.

Channels that appeared only occasionally, or only in one condition, were kept on a watch-list unless they later dominated the averaged outputs.

### Artefact rejection
Artefact rejection was run using SPM `spm_eeg_artefact` with a participant-specific threshold. The threshold was chosen as approximately the 97.5th percentile of maximum absolute trial amplitude across currently good MEG channels.

SPM artefact settings:

```text
mode: reject
badchanthresh: 0.2
append: true
channels: MEG
method: threshchan
excwin: 400 ms
prefix: a
```

### Robust averaging
Robust condition-wise averaging was performed after artefact rejection.

```text
robust averaging: on
ks: 3
bycondition: 1
savew: 1
removebad: 1
plv: 0
prefix: m
```

### Additional averaged-output QC
After robust averaging, the three condition averages were inspected visually. When averages looked suspicious, ranked-channel QC was run to identify channels with the largest maximum absolute amplitudes in each condition. Additional channels were added only when they clearly dominated the averages or appeared consistently across multiple conditions.

